// The INCONCLUSIVE guard. Run this BEFORE trusting any verdict.
//
// It answers: did the trial cohort actually receive enough requests to judge,
// and is the data fresh? An empty result is not zero errors -- it is missing
// evidence, and the contract treats the two differently on purpose.
//
// Deliberately does NOT report a duplicate count. COUNT_DISTINCT in ES|QL is
// approximate (HyperLogLog++), so requests - COUNT_DISTINCT(request_id) reads
// as ~0.8% phantom duplicates on samples this size -- an artifact that would
// wrongly trigger INCONCLUSIVE. Duplicates are structurally impossible anyway,
// because request_id is the document _id, so a repeat overwrites rather than
// double-counts. The real completeness check is the load generator's
// completed-vs-searchable reconciliation.
//
// config_hashes must be 1. More than one means the service's behaviour changed
// mid-window, which invalidates the comparison.
//
// Params: ?run_id, ?window_start, ?window_end
FROM sloproof-requests
| WHERE run_id == ?run_id AND traffic_class == "ordinary"
    AND @timestamp >= ?window_start AND @timestamp < ?window_end
| STATS requests      = COUNT(*),
        first_seen    = MIN(@timestamp),
        last_seen     = MAX(@timestamp),
        config_hashes = COUNT_DISTINCT(config_hash)
      BY version
| EVAL meets_min_samples = requests >= 400
| KEEP version, requests, meets_min_samples, config_hashes, first_seen, last_seen
| SORT version
